(2) GEOMETRIC 7-region incl-excl for ODD n: h(n) =? A+B-C+D-E-F+G
    A=B=h(n-1), C=D=h(n-2), E=F=h(n-3), G=h(n-4)
    n=5: A+B-C+D-E-F+G = 4  h(n)=4  OK
    n=7: A+B-C+D-E-F+G = 9  h(n)=9  OK
    n=9: A+B-C+D-E-F+G = 16  h(n)=16  OK
    n=11: A+B-C+D-E-F+G = 25  h(n)=25  OK
    n=13: A+B-C+D-E-F+G = 36  h(n)=36  OK

(3) COMPLEMENT-INVARIANCE of tournament invariants (reverse all arcs):
   n=4 (64 tournaments): c3(T)=c3(T^op) in 64/64; HP(T)=HP(T^op) in 64/64; score-complement law in 64/64
   n=5 (1024 tournaments): c3(T)=c3(T^op) in 1024/1024; HP(T)=HP(T^op) in 1024/1024; score-complement law in 1024/1024
   n=6 (32768 tournaments): c3(T)=c3(T^op) in 32768/32768; HP(T)=HP(T^op) in 32768/32768; score-complement law in 32768/32768

   => c3, HP complement-INVARIANT (so summable over the half-region); scores complement to (n-1)-s.
   => SC tournaments (T iso T^op) = self-paired = the diagonal {x+y=n+1} spine.
